WEBVTT

00:02:28.477 --> 00:02:31.230
to take a bite out of this 
growing problem.

00:02:31.439 --> 00:02:36.319
In 2016, a team of Japanese researchers 
sampling sludge

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:39.322
at a plastic-bottle recycling plant 
discovered

00:02:39.322 --> 00:02:43.701
Ideonella sakaiensis 201-F6.

00:02:43.951 --> 00:02:48.789
This never-before-identified bacterium 
contained two enzymes

00:02:48.789 --> 00:02:53.169
capable of slowly breaking 
down PET polymers

00:02:53.169 --> 00:02:55.338
at relatively low temperatures.

00:02:55.504 --> 00:03:00.551
Researchers isolated the genes coding 
for these plastic-digesting enzymes,